<main id="main" class="wrap ai-main" data-bundle="@@BUNDLE@@" data-revision="@@REVISION@@">
<header class="ref-head"><p class="eyebrow">Build with Nexo / AI Guide</p><h1>A small prompt.<br>A grounded starting point.</h1><p class="lede">Give your assistant the Nexo syntax, engineering habits and feature boundaries it needs. Start compact; expand documentation when the task calls for it. No backend, account or API key is required.</p><p>Python package @@PYTHON@@ · Rust workspace @@RUST@@ · API edition @@EDITION@@</p><p class="revision">Source revision <code>@@REVISION@@</code></p></header>
<section aria-labelledby="compose"><h2 id="compose">Choose your context</h2>
<div class="ai-controls"><label for="profile">Profile</label><select id="profile" disabled><option value="developer">Nexo Developer</option><option value="beginner">Beginner-friendly</option><option value="architect">Software Architect + SRE + Security</option><option value="agentic">AI/Agentic Engineer</option></select>
<label for="experience">Your experience</label><select id="experience" disabled><option value="beginner">Beginner — guided choices</option><option value="developer" selected>Developer — options and trade-offs</option><option value="expert">Expert — constraints and operations</option></select><label for="context-version">Documentation version</label><select id="context-version" disabled><option value="@@BUNDLE@@">Current — @@REVISION@@</option></select><p id="version-status" role="status"></p>
<fieldset disabled id="mode"><legend>Context</legend><label><input type="radio" name="mode" value="compact" checked> Compact</label><label><input type="radio" name="mode" value="full"> Full Context</label></fieldset>
<fieldset disabled id="access"><legend>Documentation access</legend><label><input type="radio" name="access" value="offline" checked> Self-contained / offline</label><label><input type="radio" name="access" value="url"> Model can open URLs</label></fieldset></div>
<p id="context-help">Compact includes essential rules and syntax. Full Context includes a curated evidence pack, not the entire repository. URL prompts require the model to retrieve documentation.</p>
<label for="prompt">Prompt to copy — append your task</label><textarea id="prompt" readonly spellcheck="false" rows="18" aria-describedby="context-help measurement">@@PROMPT@@</textarea>
<div class="ai-actions"><button id="copy-prompt" type="button">Copy Prompt</button><a id="download-prompt" href="@@DEFAULT_DOWNLOAD@@" download>Download prompt</a><span id="token-count" data-tokens="@@TOKENS@@">@@TOKENS@@ reference tokens</span></div>
<p id="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p><p id="measurement" class="ref-note">Measured with tiktoken 0.12.0 / cl100k_base. Counts cover the prompt text only; they exclude fetched documents, your task and chat overhead. Other providers may tokenize differently. Current-page full evidence pack: @@FULL_TOKENS@@ reference tokens.</p>
<p>Browser UI tasks: <a href="@@BUNDLE@@/nexo-web.txt">Nexo Web M1–M2 guidance and compiler-verified projects</a>. Typed props, pages, layouts, slots, routing and context are experimental M2; browser APIs remain proposed. <a href="web.html">Documentation and working demo</a>.</p>
<noscript><p>The default prompt is ready to select and copy manually. JavaScript enables profile switching, clipboard feedback and local review forms. All variants are available in the bundle below.</p></noscript></section>
<section aria-labelledby="readiness-heading"><h2 id="readiness-heading">Start with five useful answers</h2><p>Answer what you know. Leave gaps blank. Your text stays in this browser; copy the report separately into your assistant. These answers are not included in the canonical prompt or its token count.</p>
@@QUESTIONS@@
<button type="button" id="make-readiness">Create project readiness brief</button><label for="project-report">Project readiness report — select to copy</label><textarea id="project-report" readonly rows="8"></textarea></section>
<section aria-labelledby="examples-heading"><h2 id="examples-heading">Verified Nexo examples</h2><p>Recorded Python interpreter checks and local test/execution results. Native compilation is unverified. Filter by feature or engineering domain; no provider calls or external broker is needed.</p><label for="example-search">Search examples</label><input id="example-search" type="search" placeholder="Try agent, database, window, API or contracts"><p id="example-status" role="status">Five examples available.</p><p><a href="@@BUNDLE@@/examples.json">Versioned machine-readable catalog</a></p>@@EXAMPLES@@</section>
<details><summary>Architecture, ADRs and deterministic workflow</summary><p><a href="@@BUNDLE@@/engineering.txt">Task-specific engineering guidance</a> covers readiness, the simplest sufficient architecture, reliability, observability, security, local kind/k3d testing and budget-aware hosting comparisons.</p><p>Requirements → Architecture → ADRs → Implementation → Compilation → Tests → Security Review → Performance Validation → Deployment. Generated prompts are reproducible; LLM responses are not.</p><h3>Draft an ADR</h3><p>Drafts are Proposed. Save approved records in your project’s existing ADR location or <code>docs/adr/</code>. This page never approves a decision.</p>@@ADR_FIELDS@@<button type="button" id="make-adr">Draft Proposed ADR</button><label for="adr-report">ADR draft — select to copy</label><textarea id="adr-report" readonly rows="8"></textarea></details>
<details><summary>Production readiness assessment</summary><p>Equal category weights: Passed = 1, Failed/Unknown = 0. Evidence is required for Passed and Not applicable; evidenced N/A is excluded. All N/A gives no score. Critical Failed/Unknown items block regardless of score. Evidence is user-supplied and needs review; this is not certification.</p><div id="readiness-categories"></div><button id="score-readiness" type="button" disabled>Assess readiness</button><label for="production-report">Readiness assessment</label><textarea id="production-report" readonly rows="10"></textarea><p><a href="@@BUNDLE@@/readiness.json">Scoring rubric</a></p></details>
<details><summary>Local token and cost comparison</summary><p>The selected prompt has a measured cl100k_base count. Supply baseline/output reference counts and your current prices; target-provider counts and costs are estimates. No keys, model calls or private-data uploads. Use the local profiler to tokenize full input/output transcripts and count correction iterations.</p><label for="baseline-tokens">Baseline input tokens</label><input id="baseline-tokens" type="number" min="0"><label for="output-tokens">Output token allowance for both prompts</label><input id="output-tokens" type="number" min="0" value="0"><label for="input-rate">Input price per million tokens (your currency)</label><input id="input-rate" type="number" min="0" step="any"><label for="output-rate">Output price per million tokens (same currency)</label><input id="output-rate" type="number" min="0" step="any"><button id="estimate-cost" type="button">Compare estimated cost</button><p id="cost-report" role="status"></p><p><a href="https://github.com/marcrabadan/nexo/blob/main/docs/ai-guide/README.md">Local profiler and paired benchmark instructions</a>. No AI improvement results have been measured by this site.</p></details>
<details><summary>Generic coding-agent instructions</summary><p><a href="@@BUNDLE@@/agent-instructions.txt">Download canonical generic agent guidance</a>. It covers fundamentals, tools, testing, architecture, Shield, reliability, deployment and AI workflows through selective references. Guidance is not verified compiler behavior. Tool-specific adapters are deferred until their formats are documented and validated.</p></details>
<section><h2>Know the boundaries</h2><p>Use this as assistance, not a certification. A passing check does not prove runtime permissions, kernel isolation, production readiness or correct model behavior. Roadmap items are not available APIs.</p>@@CLAIMS@@</section>
<details><summary>Shield Security Assessment</summary><p>Every architecture and readiness review assesses Shield as the preferred security foundation. Start with least privilege; verify workload and host compatibility before choosing API enforcement, Linux offline/online workers or hardened Docker. Required isolation must never silently fall back.</p><p><a href="@@BUNDLE@@/shield-security.txt">Open the versioned security checklist and profile limits</a>. Report the recommendation, capabilities, execution profile, unsupported operations, isolation limits, validation commands and remaining risks. Load this detail only when relevant; offline assistants can ask you to supply its text. Shield complements Kubernetes and infrastructure controls.</p></details>
<details><summary>Documentation, downloads and progressive context</summary><p>For models with browsing, start with the compact index and fetch only the relevant documents. For offline models, choose the self-contained prompt. Full Context is curated and may exceed your model’s context window.</p><ul><li><a href="@@BUNDLE@@/llms.txt">Versioned llms.txt index</a></li><li><a href="@@BUNDLE@@/llms-full.txt">Full curated evidence pack</a></li><li><a href="@@BUNDLE@@/nexo-syntax.txt">Compact syntax reference</a></li><li><a href="@@BUNDLE@@/manifest.json">Sources, hashes and measurements</a></li><li><a href="@@BUNDLE@@/prompts.json">All prompt variants (JSON)</a></li></ul>@@DOWNLOADS@@</details>
<details><summary>How versions and measurements work</summary><p>The content revision hashes the guide rules, generator, page assets and selected repository evidence. Identical inputs produce identical prompts. Existing snapshots are retained when context changes. Package versions describe different components, not a stable Nexo 1.0 release.</p><p>The llms.txt format is a <a href="https://llmstxt.org/">documentation discovery proposal</a>; automatic adoption by an LLM is not guaranteed. Token counts use the documented <a href="https://github.com/openai/tiktoken">tiktoken tokenizer</a>, not a universal token estimate. See the <a href="https://github.com/marcrabadan/nexo/blob/main/docs/ai-guide/README.md">maintenance guide</a>.</p></details>
